API-08: convert swmm_node_set_quality_mass_flux from mass/sec like [INFLOWS] MASS

swmm_node_set_quality_mass_flux() is documented as mass/sec in project mass
units (mg/s for a MG/L pollutant) but stored the rate unconverted, and the
quality loader adds it to the node's inflow mass, which is in concentration
x cfs. [INFLOWS] MASS divides by L_PER_FT3 for that reason (Inflow.cpp), so
the API delivered 28.317 times the requested mass. Divide by the same
constant, which gives the same numbers as the patched legacy engine.

test_ard_transport passed kC0 as the forcing rate, meaning 1 cfs x kC0 in
internal units; it now passes the same load in mg/s (28.317 x kC0).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-08_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/openswmm_nodes_impl.cpp b/src/engine/core/openswmm_nodes_impl.cpp
index 8cd649f..e33031b 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/openswmm_nodes_impl.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/openswmm_nodes_impl.cpp
@@ -397,7 +397,9 @@ SWMM_ENGINE_API int swmm_node_set_quality_mass_flux(SWMM_Engine engine, int node
         ctx.nodes.user_conc_mass_flux.resize(
             static_cast<std::size_t>(ctx.n_nodes()) * static_cast<std::size_t>(np), 0.0);
     }
-    ctx.nodes.user_conc_mass_flux[flat] = mass_rate;
+    // mass/sec to internal (concen. x cfs), as Inflow.cpp does for [INFLOWS] MASS
+    constexpr double L_PER_FT3 = 28.317;   // legacy consts.h LperFT3
+    ctx.nodes.user_conc_mass_flux[flat] = mass_rate / L_PER_FT3;
     return SWMM_OK;
 }
 
diff --git a/tests/unit/engine/test_ard_transport.cpp b/tests/unit/engine/test_ard_transport.cpp
